# Karpathy rules (observed by A. Karpathy, codified by Forrest Chang)

1. Think before coding — state assumptions, ask if ambiguous, surface tradeoffs.
2. Simplicity first — minimum code; no speculative abstractions; if 200 lines could be 50, rewrite.
3. Surgical changes — every changed line traces to the request; don't touch adjacent code; mention (don't delete) pre-existing dead code.
4. Goal-driven — define a verifiable success criterion before coding; loop until it passes.

# Sentinel hard rule

The final pass/fail gate is DETERMINISTIC code. LLM stages output scores + evidence ONLY — never the decision.

# Project

Python 3.12 / FastAPI; vanilla HTML/JS UI (no framework). Files < 400 lines; immutable data.
No new npm installs (supply-chain freeze). `contracts.py` is the interface — import, don't edit.
